From 99af99046c7a385bfbdc75c1472ba7943e1a5645 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:38:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 63/64] History works in every tab when another tab's history
 read hangs

Up-arrow history read the shell's history file once per user/host/shell, through the first
session that bootstrapped; every other session waited on that read. In embedded builds the read
is an in-band `cat` in that session's shell, and it can hang for good: a shell taken over after a
page reload while it runs a command (`tail -f`, Claude Code) drops Warp's writes, so the `cat`
never runs. Until it does, every tab's history menu showed "No results", even for commands just
run there. Now each session that bootstraps while the read is in progress reads the file too,
and the first read to finish is used.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
